---
title: Week to Week
---

# Week to Week

The Week to Week report answers the question "how does each day of the week
compare?". It draws each day of the week as its own line, on one 24-hour axis.

## What it shows

The chart has seven lines, one for each day of the week, from Sunday to
Saturday. The horizontal axis is the time of day. The vertical axis is your
glucose. The key under the chart names the line for each day.

Where the lines are close together, your days are alike at that time. Where
one line is far from the others, that day of the week is different.

If the period is longer than one week, each line shows the average for that day
of the week. For example, the Monday line is the average of all the Mondays in
the period.

The app shows glucose values in mmol/L if you chose mmol/L.

## How to use it

The report opens on the last 7 days. To compare this week with the week before:

1. Look at the chart for this week. Find the times when one day is different.
2. Select the left arrow above the chart. The chart moves back one week.
3. Compare the same times on the chart for last week.
4. To move forward one week, select the right arrow.
5. To go back to the current week, select **Reset**.

You can also open a week from the [Year Overview](/docs/reports/year-overview):
select a week number under the calendar.

## Good to know

- The arrows always move by 7 days. They start from the first or last day of
  the period on the screen.
- If a week has no readings, the chart shows **No data available for this
  week**.
